              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Active 300 (SF-T724011)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$499.99, sold out</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$599.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Store cheaper when in stock</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Amazon also listed Sunny models we could not tie to a single store listing: a TreadPad compact treadmill with a
            remote at $289.99, a TreadPad with 7% auto incline and handlebar at $516.51, a 15% <a href="/best-auto-incline-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>auto-incline treadmill</a> with a
            20-inch running surface at $1,025.99, a Wi-Fi treadmill with a 10-inch touchscreen at $883.56, and a
            commercial-level incline-decline treadmill at $2,999.99, the same figure as the SF-X7200 on Sunny’s store.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two cautions. Amazon prices on Sunny listings move daily and some are sold by third parties, so check the
            seller and the SF number in the listing before you buy. And the store and Amazon do not always describe the
            same model the same way: our Sunny guide found the T4400SMART hard to locate on Amazon by its model number,
            for example. Match the <a href="/treadmill-belt-size-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>belt size</a>, speed, incline and weight limit, not just the photo.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="black-friday" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Is There a Sunny Black Friday Sale on Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            Sunny’s store ran a Black Friday banner on 27 November 2026 reading “BLACK FRIDAY IS HERE!” and “SAVE UP TO
            $600!”, linking to a Black Friday and Cyber Monday 2026 deals page. That page featured one-day deals on smaller
            equipment, such as a Roman chair, an ab trainer and a mini <a href="/best-exercise-bikes/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>exercise bike</a>, scheduled through 29 November.
          </p>
          <p>
            What we could not find was a visible treadmill discount. Almost none of Sunny’s treadmill listings carried a
            “was” price in the store’s product data that day; the exceptions were the Asuna space-saving models ($549.99 and
            $599.99 against $699.99) and two sold-out machines. The “up to $600” claim may apply to other equipment or to
            savings shown only in the cart, which we did not test. So treat the prices in the tables above as Sunny’s
            current prices, not as a sale, and compare them with Amazon, where most models were cheaper on the same day.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are shopping the holiday sales across brands, our <a href="/treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Black Friday treadmill deals</a> and <a href="/black-friday-treadmill-deals-under-500/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Black Friday deals under $500</a> pages cover the budget tier
            where most Sunny models sit, and our <a href="/cyber-monday-walking-pad-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cyber Monday walking pad deals</a> page tracks the pads Sunny’s TreadPads compete with.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="what-money-buys" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What the Extra Money Buys at Each Sunny Price</h2>
<p>
            Sunny’s range climbs in small steps, and most steps add one feature. A rough guide to what each band buys,
            from Sunny’s listing titles and our Sunny guide:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[560px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price band (store)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">What you get</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Who it suits</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $200</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">A non-electric manual walker with a fixed incline</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Short walks where no outlet is handy</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$300–$450</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">A flat TreadPad walking pad, or a basic folding treadmill</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Desk walking or easy home walking</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$450–$600</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Incline (manual, then automatic), handlebar 2-in-1 pads, Wi-Fi and the SunnyFit app</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Walkers who want more effort without more speed</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$600–$800</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20-inch belts, low decks, flat folding, higher weight limits</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Joggers, taller users, small rooms</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,000–$1,200</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Decline, touchscreens and the 20-inch Astra Elite</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Hill walkers and regular runners on a budget</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,200–$3,000</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Steep incline-decline trainers and a curved manual treadmill</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Hill training and sprint work</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Two notes from our Sunny guide apply across the range. Sunny states motor power as a peak figure, which tells
            you less than a continuous rating, so compare belt size and weight limit instead. And the cheapest models have
            the lowest published weight limits; if you are near a model’s limit, step up to one of the 300 lb-rated machines,
            such as the 20-inch SF-T723016 at $799.99, rather than the cheapest pad. For an incline-decline machine at a lower price, our <a href="/best-treadmills-with-decline/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmills with decline</a> roundup compares Sunny with other brands.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="warranty-returns" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Warranty, Returns and What Parts Cost</h2>
<p>
            Our Sunny guide recorded that Sunny’s store lists a three-year frame warranty and 180 days on parts for its <a href="/folding-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>folding treadmills</a>, and that the warranty reads differently on some product pages than on the policy page.
            Check the warranty tab on the exact model before buying, and register it when it arrives. A 180-day parts term
            is short: a motor control board failing in month seven is your cost.
          </p>
          <p>
            That makes the price of common parts part of the cost of ownership. Sunny’s store listed these on 27
            November 2026:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Part (Sunny store)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price (27 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">When you need it</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmill lubricant, 20 ml</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$5.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Routine belt care; see our walking pad lubrication guide</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmill safety key</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$12.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lost or broken key</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmill emergency brake clip</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$9.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lost clip</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmill power cord</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$19.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Damaged cord</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Equipment mat, small (Amazon)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$19.37</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Floor protection and noise</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Sunny’s banner also said it now accepts HSA and FSA payments. Whether a treadmill qualifies usually depends on
            a medical reason; our <a href="/are-treadmills-hsa-fsa-eligible/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">HSA and FSA guide</a> explains how that works.
            For returns, Sunny publishes its terms on its store; compare them with other brands in our <a href="/treadmill-return-policies/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill return policies</a> guide, and note that an Amazon purchase
            follows Amazon’s return window and the seller’s terms instead. Keeping a pad lubricated is the cheapest repair:
            see <a href="/how-to-lubricate-a-walking-pad/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how to lubricate a walking pad</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="vs-rivals" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Sunny vs UREVO, WalkingPad, Horizon and NordicTrack at the Same Money</h2>
<p>
            Sunny competes mostly with Amazon walking-pad brands below $600 and with Horizon and NordicTrack’s entry
            treadmills above it. Using prices recorded on our own pages:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[600px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Machine</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price (source, date)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Notes</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sunny Treadpad 100</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$242.22 (Amazon, 27 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Flat walking pad, Wi-Fi</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">UREVO Strol 2E Pro</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$171.99 (UREVO, 27 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Walking pad with 12% manual incline and handle</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">WalkingPad Z1</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$265.04 (Amazon, 27 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">47.6 in. belt, folds in half</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sunny SF-T7718 Strider</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$565.00 (Amazon, 27 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Low deck, 20 in. belt, flat folding</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">NordicTrack T Series 5</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$419–$590 (our Cyber Monday page)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">iFIT-ready entry treadmill</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Horizon T101 Connect</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $699–$700 (our Cyber Monday page)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Folding, longer warranty</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Under $300, UREVO and WalkingPad pads were cheaper than Sunny’s on Black Friday, and UREVO’s store was
            discounting more visibly. Between $550 and $800, Sunny’s case is the range of low-deck, 20-inch and auto-incline
            options, but the Horizon T101 is the one to compare on warranty before you buy. Our <a href="/how-much-does-a-urevo-walking-pad-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">UREVO walking pad cost</a>, <a href="/how-much-does-a-walking-pad-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">walking pad cost</a> and <a href="/how-much-does-a-horizon-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon cost</a> guides have the details.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="cheapest" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>How to Pay Less for a Sunny Treadmill</h2>
<ul>
            <li><strong>Check Amazon by SF number.</strong> On 27 November Amazon was $20 to $500 cheaper on five of the
            six models we matched.</li>
            <li><strong>Do not wait for a Sunny store discount on treadmills.</strong> Its Black Friday banner did not
            translate into visible treadmill reductions in the store’s product data.</li>
            <li><strong>Buy the feature you will use.</strong> Auto incline adds about $50 to $150 over manual incline on
            similar Sunny pads and folding treadmills; decline and a touchscreen roughly double the price.</li>
            <li><strong>Watch sold-out models.</strong> Several mid-range machines were sold out; when they return, compare
            their price with the in-stock alternatives above.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For most buyers the realistic Sunny budget is $250 to $650 at Amazon prices: a TreadPad for desk walking or an
            SF-T7718 or 20-inch auto-incline model for jogging. Spend more only for decline or a steep incline, and spend less
            only if you want a manual walker.
          </p>
        </div>


        <!-- Common mistakes -->
        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Where People Go Wrong When Pricing a Sunny Treadmill</h2>
          <p>Sunny’s range is wide and its names are long, so most overpaying comes from matching the wrong model or the wrong store.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Buying on the store without checking Amazon</h3>
              <p>Amazon was cheaper on five of six models we matched on 27 November, by up to $500.99. Search the SF number on Amazon before you check out.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Comparing by photo instead of model number</h3>
              <p>Sunny sells many similar-looking machines. Match the SF number, belt size, incline and weight limit before you compare two prices.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Choosing the cheapest model when you are heavier</h3>
              <p>The cheapest pads and treadmills carry the lowest weight limits. If you are near the limit, step up to a 300 lb-rated machine.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Ignoring the short parts warranty</h3>
              <p>Our Sunny guide recorded 180 days on parts. Budget for parts after that, keep the belt lubricated, and register the machine on arrival.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- The bottom line -->
        <div id="bottom-line" class="ed-bottomline">
          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">A Sunny treadmill costs $199.99 to $2,999.99 on its store, and most buyers will pay $250 to $650.</strong> On 27 November 2026 Sunny’s store priced TreadPad walking pads at $299.99 to $599.99 and folding motorised
            treadmills at $399.99 to $799.99, with no visible treadmill discount despite a Black Friday banner.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Check Amazon by SF number before you buy.</strong> Amazon was cheaper on most models we
            matched, by $20 to $500. Match the belt, incline and weight limit to how you will use it, and read our <a href="/sunny-health-fitness-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Sunny treadmill guide</a> for the figures that conflict between listings.
          </p>
